rust-proxmox-deb-version (0.1.1-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * compare a version without a Debian revision like dpkg does, as if it had
    an empty one, so 1.0 equals 1.0-0 and is newer than a backport like
    1.0-0~bpo1.

  * make equality agree with the ordering, so versions that compare as equal,
    like 1.01 and 1.1, are also equal for ==.

  * add strict validation of versions, rejecting what dpkg --validate-version
    rejects, with the reason, and normalizing them like dpkg does. This suits
    versions entered by users.

 -- Proxmox Support Team <support@proxmox.com>  Wed, 18 Nov 2026 02:32:15 +0100

